# Every repo in the org calls the reusable workflows in this directory, and they run with
# `id-token: write` (Infisical OIDC) plus pull-request and issue write. A change here executes
# with those privileges in ~28 repositories, so it is the highest-leverage path in the org and
# must not land by direct push.
#
# This is the control that lets the callers keep `@main`: the shared workflow stays instantly
# fixable everywhere, and the change itself is what gets reviewed. Pinning 28 callers to a SHA
# would invert that, freezing each repo on whatever was current the day it was created and
# requiring 28 merges to ship a security fix.

.github/workflows/   @ryaniosys/engineering
